Linux backend fallback: register shortcuts even when the webview never
loads. The frontend normally calls initialize_shortcuts after the UI
boots, but the box-built AppImage's bundled WebKit EGL-aborts on the
Fedora host, so the call never came and ctrl+space stayed dead
(2026-07-17). initialize_shortcuts is idempotent, so backend + frontend
both calling it is safe. Applies on top of patches 01-04.

--- a/src-tauri/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src-tauri/src/lib.rs
@@ -571,6 +571,21 @@
                 show_main_window(&app_handle);
             }
 
+            // Linux: the frontend calls initialize_shortcuts once the webview
+            // loads, but a broken webview (e.g. bundled WebKit EGL-aborting on
+            // the host) must not leave dictation dead. The command is
+            // idempotent, so this backend fallback is safe alongside it.
+            #[cfg(target_os = "linux")]
+            {
+                let handle = app_handle.clone();
+                std::thread::spawn(move || {
+                    std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_secs(3));
+                    if let Err(e) = crate::commands::initialize_shortcuts(handle) {
+                        log::error!("Backend fallback shortcut init failed: {}", e);
+                    }
+                });
+            }
+
             Ok(())
         })
         .on_window_event(|window, event| match event {
